Month = {AUG},
Abstract = {This paper is concerned with the determination of total negative ion
   number density (n\_) in a dc plasma discharge of N2O employing laser
   induced photo-detachment coupled with an electrostatic Langmuir probe.
   Electrons resulting from the photo-detachment are investigated and used
   to evaluate the negative ion number density employing the electron
   energy distribution function (EEDF) using the recorded I-V
   characteristic curves. The electron temperature was found to be
   dependent on pressure at the lowest discharge power, while it seems to
   be almost independent of discharge pressure at discharge powers higher
   than 10 000 mW. The negative ion number density was found to increase
   linearly as a function of discharge power within the 10(13)m(-3) scale
   and also increase as a function of pressure. The electro-negativity of
   N2O was found to be about 0.03 at the lowest pressure and the lowest
   discharge power.},
