Title = {Introduction to Networked Control Systems},
Booktitle = {CONTROL STRATEGIES AND CO-DESIGN OF NETWORKED CONTROL SYSTEMS:
   CONSIDERING TIME DELAY EFFECTS},
Series = {Modeling and Optimization in Science and Technologies},
Year = {2019},
Volume = {13},
Pages = {1-23},
Abstract = {This chapter introduces a brief description of Networked Control
   Systems. A formal review of this book is given, describing the key
   issues within each chapter. A review of the strategies present in the
   literature is made to study and compensate for the network imperfections
   presenting three main methodologies. The control methodology focuses on
   generating control signals that counteract the effects of the network
   imperfections through modelling its dynamics or considering them as
   uncertainties. The communication methodology aims to improve the
   transmission of information and minimise imperfections through the
   scheduling and synchronisation of the nodes present in the network as a
   function of the system performance. The co-design methodology considers
   increasing the advantages of the various methodologies with the purpose
   of increasing system performance and minimising the effects of network
   imperfections. It is also presented the time delay modelling in
   nondeterministic networks, the main imperfection of the network.
   Finally, the maximum allowed transfer interval term is described which
   is the maximum bound for time imperfections of the network.},
