Abstract = {Prockia jaliscana is described and illustrated as a new species from the
   state of Jalisco, Mexico. This species is similar to P. oaxacana;
   however, it differs from the latter because it is dioecious, presents
   linear or lanceolate to foliaceous stipules, has male and female flowers
   different from those of P. oxacana, apetalous staminate flowers and
   presents an ovary with ovules in both basal and parietal placentae.},
