Abstract = {A revision of Palmanura is presented, P. klompeni sp. nov. P. moralesi
   sp. nov., P. contrerasi sp. nov. and P. axelretanai sp. nov. are
   described and illustrated, and P. normae Palacios-Vargas, 1996 and P.
   sernai Palacios-Vargas \& Simon Benito, 2009 are redescribed. New
   records and distribution data are given for several species and a key
   for identifying every species of the genus are included. A discussion on
   the ventral chaetotaxy of all genera of the tribe Sensillanurini and a
   comparison with other tribes of Neanurinae is also provided.},
